  "event_seq": 101,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to 1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-03). The majority (59%, E-02) of disputed bills were built from ACTUAL meter reads rather than estimates, and no tariff change occurred (E-04), so the surge is driven primarily by a billing-side defect in processing/validating accepted actual reads downstream of read collection - not by field-read/estimation shortfalls, which affect only a minority (41%, E-02) of disputes despite a real route-completion shortfall (0.88 vs 0.95 target, E-01) - and not by slow dispute response, which remains within SLA (E-05)."
